{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1119577-project-twilight-inspirational-media","id":1119577,"title":"Project: Twilight Inspirational Media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-23T11:07:33-07:00","id":1119577,"title":"Project: Twilight Inspirational Media","content":"So, all the main game lines seem to have inspirational media threads, so I figured I'd try one for one of the small fries. In this case, the FBI Special Affairs Division/Project: Twilight breed of government agents investigating paranormal events and supernatural monsters. <br /> <br /> <b>The X-Files: </b>Getting the most obvious one out of the way first. Effectively the benchmark for the genre. While the &quot;metaplot&quot; episodes often made little sense (as they were more or less making it up as they went along) and Mulder would sometimes come across as a complete idiot (&quot;I saw something vague so it <i>must</i> be this weird fringe thing!&quot; &quot;But you don't have any physical evidence that you saw it.&quot; &quot;WHO GOT TO YOU! ARE YOU PART OF THE CONSPIRACY!!!&quot;), but a lot of the monster-of-the-week episodes are pretty good, and the bureaucratic red tape and political skullduggery within the Bureau is something an SAD centered game should take into account, IMO. <br /> <br /> <b>Ultraviolet</b><b>:</b> This was a one-season British show from the same period about the official group who deal with vampires in Britain. If you've never seen it, it's pretty good, featuring Idris Elba in one of his earlier roles, and doing a totally scientific take on vampirism. <br /> <br /> <b>Thomas Harris's Red Dragon and The Silence of the Lambs:</b> The books that helped popularize criminal profiling and introduced the world to Hannibal Lecter, both being made into films (Red Dragon was originally made in the 80s as Manhunter, so it makes an interesting compare and contrast with the more recent version).<br /> <br /> <b>Thunderheart: </b>1992 movie with Val Kilmer as an FBI agent investigating a murder on Sioux land. There are no supernatural elements, but the politics, corruption and conspiracy angles all fit in with the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Criminal Minds: </b>The long running TV series about the FBI behavior analysis unit. <br /> <br /> Any more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T11:38:50-07:00","id":1119586,"title":"","content":"Probably a lot of things that can be taken from an episode of Stranger Things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T12:44:46-07:00","id":1119604,"title":"","content":"the Aldrich Ames case. was